S164 LRC14 CERTIFICATE HANDOFF ATLAS
========================================================================
Assumption challenge: vertices are proof carriers / obligations, not runners.
Pairwise observable: retained LRC predicate payload across handoffs.

Carrier tournament
------------------
score_hist: {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 4: 3, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1}
directed_3cycles: 1
SCC_sizes: [1, 1, 3, 1, 1, 1, 1]
Hamiltonian_path_count: 3
tie/retention Hamiltonian path:
  labelled_source_packet > exact_interval_fejer > ramanujan_exact_period > endpoint_bridge_graph > twist_ladder_blocker > danger_count_moment_dual > analytic_sieve_kaczynski > tournament_state_lift > raw_scalar_shadow

Carrier roles
-------------
- labelled_source_packet: vector=(5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 4, 4, 5)
  role=root sheaf: qdiv/Farey/Haar/endpoint/C27/K33/state labels
  must_retain=qdiv, exact_M_Farey, strict_vs_boundary, endpoint_owners, route
  may_forget=raw runner order after packet key is fixed
- exact_interval_fejer: vector=(5, 5, 4, 4, 3, 5, 5, 5, 4)
  role=formal dual certificate target: Q_d(center)<0 on packet fibers
  must_retain=packet_key, center, degree, atom_formula, interval_upper
  may_forget=floating decimal shadow, raw endpoint list after center/component is fixed
- ramanujan_exact_period: vector=(4, 4, 5, 3, 2, 4, 4, 4, 4)
  role=primitive phase projector and late-q pre-splitter
  must_retain=q, unit_residue, weak_vs_strict_witness, route_label
  may_forget=speed names inside a primitive residue profile
- endpoint_bridge_graph: vector=(4, 4, 3, 5, 5, 4, 4, 4, 4)
  role=taut/positive bridge layer over danger endpoints
  must_retain=left_owner, right_owner, bridge_sign, winding_or_potential
  may_forget=global scalar safe mass after bridges are labelled
- twist_ladder_blocker: vector=(4, 4, 4, 3, 2, 3, 5, 5, 4)
  role=primal rational witness or finite speed-vs-twist blocker
  must_retain=denominator_ladder, failed_twist_hypergraph, first_q
  may_forget=continuous endpoint geometry after a twist witness is found
- danger_count_moment_dual: vector=(4, 3, 2, 4, 1, 3, 5, 5, 3)
  role=count-distribution Farkas/Delsarte dual
  must_retain=count_histogram, dual_polynomial, degree, sign
  may_forget=endpoint ownership, phase position
- analytic_sieve_kaczynski: vector=(3, 4, 4, 3, 2, 4, 3, 3, 5)
  role=large-sieve/circle-method/Kaczynski boundary middle certificate
  must_retain=smoothing_kernel, exceptional_set, approach_class, exact_period_labels
  may_forget=raw prime or Mobius scalar
- tournament_state_lift: vector=(5, 3, 2, 2, 4, 5, 4, 5, 5)
  role=terminal forbidden-H=7 state-lift endpoint
  must_retain=packet_value, H(T)=7, conflict_tournament, realizability_map
  may_forget=metric values after the conflict packet is built
- raw_scalar_shadow: vector=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1)
  role=unsafe summary: tau/sigma/raw mass/raw tournament class
  must_retain=lost_label_certificate

Packet handoff table
--------------------
- packet=qdiv<14 / direct q-witness
  labelled_source_packet -> twist_ladder_blocker
  status=closed in the current grammar
  retained_predicate=existence of a strict rational witness
  destroyed_without_guard=endpoint-owner route
  open_arrow=global reduction must put every direct-witness packet here before scalarizing
- packet=AP/Goddyn-Wong boundary atom
  endpoint_bridge_graph -> labelled_source_packet
  status=equality atom, not a strict counterexample
  retained_predicate=zero strict-open mass with q=14 boundary owner skeleton
  destroyed_without_guard=C27/GW hidden acceleration, closed boundary support
  open_arrow=tight-locus census still must show no other global equality atom
- packet=K33 / 12->36 and K33 splices
  labelled_source_packet -> exact_interval_fejer
  status=selected packet certified negative; state-lift endpoint remains theorem target
  retained_predicate=positive safe interval or forbidden K33/H=7 conflict packet
  destroyed_without_guard=state-lift owner labels, K33 incidence address
  open_arrow=prove K33 family compression or construct the HYP-2908 state lift
- packet=unit petal and P10+GW strip
  labelled_source_packet -> exact_interval_fejer
  status=selected P10+GW certified negative; C27 petal route available
  retained_predicate=positive safe interval in the unit-petal packet
  destroyed_without_guard=C27 unit-hole label, two-block splice order
  open_arrow=prove the petal/two-block family template, not just named rows
- packet=covering boundary-moment packets
  endpoint_bridge_graph -> exact_interval_fejer
  status=selected covering rows certified; full family needs multi-chart positivity
  retained_predicate=strict safe component or positive boundary-moment image
  destroyed_without_guard=apex lift section, moment chart, endpoint transition packet
  open_arrow=build multi-chart gK8/L_y or Fejer family templates for all covering packets
- packet=lcm-tail / finite-denominator wall
  ramanujan_exact_period -> analytic_sieve_kaczynski
  status=q<=42 twist evidence closes audited lcm tails; global fixed basis impossible
  retained_predicate=adaptive exact-period witness or labelled Kaczynski resonance
  destroyed_without_guard=prime-power denominator labels, approach class
  open_arrow=prove dynamic ladder or admissible smoothed exponential-sum lemma
- packet=SOURCE-SPECTRUM-UNKNOWN / F7
  labelled_source_packet -> tournament_state_lift
  status=only honest falsifier bucket
  retained_predicate=simultaneous invisibility to all known primal/dual certificates
  destroyed_without_guard=which certificate failed, residual sector label
  open_arrow=define F7 and prove it is empty or constructs TournamentStateLift

Open arrows for a proof
-----------------------
- O1 source-kernel exclusion: every primitive row enters this atlas.
- O2 formal interval backend: replace prototype pi/trig intervals by checkable balls.
- O3 family compression: selected Fejer/twist certificates lift to packet templates.
- O4 admissible smoothing: analytic-sieve/Kaczynski quotients retain approach labels.
- O5 state-lift construction: any zero-open non-AP/GW residual builds HYP-2908/THM-572.
- O6 F7 definition: if a Johnson-harmonic residual sector exists, name its preserved predicate.

Fixed-margin swap-chain import
------------------------------
Source pattern: arXiv:2606.22636 reduces fixed-margin swap chains to a
low-row heat-bath core and then splits count sectors from Johnson harmonics.
- fixed margins are labels: binary row/column margins behave like packet fibers: a comparison argument may move between chains only while preserving the margin fiber or recording its kernel.
- reduce to a low-row core: the swap-chain proof reduces arbitrary margins to three rows; the LRC14 analogue is to reduce arbitrary primitive rows to a finite packet core before applying Fejer, twist, or state-lift certificates.
- split count and harmonic sectors: the three-row analysis decomposes by column count and Johnson harmonic sectors; the LRC14 F7 bucket should be defined as a named harmonic residual sector, not as an anonymous failure of existing certificates.

Zipper theorem candidate
------------------------
If O1-O6 hold, then every primitive LRC14 row either has a strict witness/dual certificate in the atlas, is the AP/GW equality atom, or constructs the forbidden HYP-2908/THM-572 state lift.  This would close LRC14.  The atlas does not prove O1-O6; it localizes them.
